## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of space-time trade-offs in streaming analysis. Introduces hashing-based approximation and how it affects accuracy, latency, and memory.

## Key Concepts
- Hash bucketing for compact counts
- Amortized batch updates
- Probability of collision vs. accuracy
- Space-time trade-offs vs. exact counting

## Code Example
```javascript
class BucketCounter {
  constructor(D) {
    this.D = D;
    this.buckets = new Array(D).fill(0);
    this.max = 0;
  }
  updateBatch(batch, hashFn) {
    for (const c of batch) {
      const b = hashFn(c) % this.D;
      this.buckets[b] += 1;
      if (this.buckets[b] > this.max) this.max = this.buckets[b];
    }
  }
  query(t) { return this.max >= t; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you bound false positives and choose D for a target ε? 
- What changes if batches vary in size or if t scales over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical thinking on append-heavy data structures, cache-aware trade-offs, and I/O modeling under realistic constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Two-tier indexing
- Amortized cost analysis
- Cache & I/O modeling
- Rebuild strategies and hot/cold separation

## Code Example
```javascript
class TieredIndex {
  constructor(B) { this.B=B; this.t1=new Map(); this.t2=new Map(); }
  append(blockId, offset) { this.t1.set(blockId, offset); /* trigger rebuild when needed */ }
  lookup(blockId) { if (this.t1.has(blockId)) return this.t1.get(blockId); return this.t2.get(blockId); }
  rebuild() { for (let [k,v] of this.t1) this.t2.set(k,v); this.t1.clear(); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would this adapt if blocks could be deleted or updated? 
- How would you empirically validate the cost model with real workloads?

